Dock cards and the move gestures.

- The `move` gesture, started on a dock pile card, moves just that card horizontally
  under the finger (live, like moving a floating window) and on release runs
  `gestures:dock_swipe_exec <l|r|none> <front>`, which features/sidedock points at
  `dock.sh gesture-move` to cycle or spring back. One gesture rather than a second
  3-finger one: Hyprland runs only the first gesture matching a finger count.
- The `float` gesture leaves dock windows alone (floating toggles break the pile).
- The scroll_move gesture drives the regular workspace when the open special
  workspace has no tiled windows (the dock's), so it keeps working with the dock open.

